WEBVTT

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.060
Can you imagine...

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:41.400
...a life in which you could
never touch the one you love?

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.230
He takes the life of whatever he touches.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.690
That was the curse the witch put on him.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.990
Plants, animals... and people
are no exception, of course.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:55.410
Regarding her son, doomed to live his life
without knowing the warmth of another,

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.080
his mother only complained.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.580
"That child is like Death incarnate..."

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.580
...she said.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.920
Morning, Alice.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:15.350
Good morning, Your Grace.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.850
I don't think you need to greet
me so up close and personal.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.980
In town this distance is the norm.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:22.980
You're making that up!

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:56.280
Episode 3
The Duke and the Meteor
 Shower During the Full Moon

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.640
You're just like a pro!

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.680
That was wonderful, Your Grace.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.230
I used to play by myself whenever
I had some spare time, so...

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.940
But are you okay with those terms?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.990
The loser has to do
whatever the winner says.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:38.410
Yes, those were the terms
I suggested, so...

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.320
Is this...

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.280
...how you hold the stick?

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.540
Well, you don't have to
lean forward so much...

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:49.370
I thought this might be more
to your liking, Your Grace.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.340
I'm not fond of any particular pose!

00:03:58.510 --> 00:03:59.510
Oh, dear!

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:03.140
Looks like this game is mine...

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.350
Alice, I'm sorry, but...

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:07.640
...I'm going to take the winning shot.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.770
Don't sink it in there.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.650
Don't sink it in there...

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:15.530
...in there ...in there ...in there.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:19.700
Uh, um, Alice, I've got to concentrate, so
could you keep quiet during the game?

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.440
Hmm, that's a foul.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.160
What?!

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.580
Alice, you may place the
ball wherever you wish.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.790
It's a safe shot from here.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.670
Looks like I won.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:37.630
Will you do whatever I ask,
like we agreed?

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.430
Well, okay... What is it?

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:44.560
What should I do if she asks me
to do something really indecent?

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.180
Would you...

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.230
...take a trip into town with me?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.230
Huh?

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.990
Are you disappointed because
it wasn't what you expected?

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.360
I'm not, I'm not!

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.450
Why do you want to go
to town all of a sudden?

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:08.080
This weekend, there's a festival.
All the townspeople will wear costumes.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.080
If your costume's thick enough,
Your Grace,

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.460
I'm sure anyone you may
bump into will be all right.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.790
B-But...

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:19.300
...I'm not used to being in
places with so many people.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:24.390
When I passed by last year,
it didn't appear to be that crowded.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.470
What do you say?

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.350
Will you go into town with me?

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.980
Don't give me that look! It's not fair!

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.150
So, this is...

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:37.320
...the town?

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.320
That's right.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.860
How's your costume working out?

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.240
It's not bad.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.740
It's a bit hard to move around in, though.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.870
By the way, that costume
looks really cute.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.290
I'm not just talking about
the outfit. You do, too.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.000
Why, thank you.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.000
Only...

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.670
...there are more people
here than I expected.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.050
Y-Yeah...

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:02.760
Hey, watch-- Yikes! Alice!

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.680
It seems I made the right call.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.680
As long as you're encased in steel,
you have nothing to worry about.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.390
But it's also heavy and
hard to keep steady...

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.390
Is everything all right, Your Grace?

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.940
Shall we go home now?

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:21.440
No, you asked me to do this, so I'll
try to hang in there a little longer.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.860
Thank you for indulging me, Your Grace.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:34.540
It may have been somewhat rash of me to
drag you to a place with so many people.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:41.670
But I've always dreamed of coming into
town like this on a date with you.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:44.970
Just like a normal couple.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.310
Your Grace?

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:55.440
I was carried away by the crowd
and got knocked over to boot.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.900
I wanna go home now.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.990
Where on earth is His Grace?

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.370
Are you Sharon? Sharon Lendrott?

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:17.420
Sharon is... my mother's name.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.670
Yes, of course, you're right.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:25.380
You startled me because you look alike,
but there's no way you could be her.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:28.930
So, you must be her daughter...
Alice, was it?

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:30.890
Who are you?

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:32.890
Nobody important.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:35.350
Just a slight acquaintance of Sharon's.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:38.850
Take care, Alice.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.860
I must go look for His Grace.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:49.160
I've wound up at a square of some sort.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.330
Where am I?

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.330
Plus...

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.910
...I've got a lost boy here
looking to me for help...

00:07:53.450 --> 00:08:01.090
Mommy!

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.920
...when I'm lost myself.

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:03.000
Don't cry so hard.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.800
It makes me feel like crying, too.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.380
Hey, there's a piano!

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:11.640
I'll play you something to cheer you up,
so dry those tears!

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:17.060
I'm so nervous.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.440
To think I'd be playing the piano
with so many people around...

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.580
Huh?

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.790
Come over here! Quick!

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.790
Hey, this is nice!

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:51.930
They're playing along with me.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.330
Yeah, that's the spirit!

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:16.700
What a wonderful tune!

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.830
Here's to the town and good music! Cheers!

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:46.610
Where have you been?

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.230
I've been worried sick about you!

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:51.700
Your mommy came for you.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:52.780
Thank goodness!

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.740
Your piano playing was so cool!

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:56.700
Bye bye!

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:57.700
Thanks!

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.000
Well now, I'd better find Alice...

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:05.380
I've found you, Your Grace.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:06.750
Alice?!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.300
Please don't go off on your own.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.960
Come on now, you're too close!

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.010
You must be getting tired.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.930
Shall we get going soon?

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:19.470
No, let's stick around a little longer.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.230
We came all this way, so...

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:24.900
...I'd like to stay here in town
with you for a bit longer.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:28.150
Your Grace, is that really you?

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:30.820
May I have a look inside your mouth?

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:32.530
Inside my mouth?! What for?!

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.940
Hey, Alice! Take a look at this!

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.270
There's a mask that looks just like me!

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.360
It certainly does.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:11.650
Right?

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:14.320
That mask was inspired
by a Death incarnate...

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:17.410
...that is said to live in
the forest north of town.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.200
Though I wouldn't know whether
such a creature actually exists.

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:23.750
Shall we be on our way now, Your Grace?

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.790
I had my suspicions all along, but...

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:32.590
...it seems there really have been strange
rumors going around about me.

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:37.050
I'm just a guy with a little
curse on him, that's all.

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:40.390
What is this? It's really good!

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:42.430
It's called ice cream.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.270
You have some too, Alice. Here.

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:46.390
All right, then.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:51.400
Why must you do it all sexy like?

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.280
Wait. We'll lose each other again.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:58.160
Your Grace, why don't we
climb the clock tower?

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.450
There doesn't appear to be
anyone up there now.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:01.450
Really?

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.290
Wow!

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:10.630
It looks like the town's
been blanketed with stars.

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:12.340
Yes, indeed.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:14.710
Alice, look! There's the moon!

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:16.970
You mustn't get so excited.
It's dangerous.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:18.220
Oh, okay.

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:30.400
Are you familiar with the town fairy tale
about the princess who marries the moon?

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:32.110
You mean, what we saw earlier?

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.110
Yes.

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:41.490
Once upon a time there lived in this land
a brave prince and a beautiful princess.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:45.910
The two were deeply in love
and engaged to be married.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:50.620
But a jealous witch took the prince
and carried him off to the moon.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.500
Help me!

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.500
I guess even in fairy tales,

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.000
all witches do is interfere.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:13:01.300
Every year since, on the
night she was to be wed,

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:04.100
the princess looks toward
the moon and offers up a kiss.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:08.480
And that's how the story goes.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:11.150
It's a rather sad tale, don't you think?

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:14.860
I'm sure the prince is also sending
her a kiss from the moon.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.610
The farthest kiss in the universe.

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:19.860
It'd be wonderful if that were the case.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:23.320
But somehow, I think that
the story describes...

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:25.410
...the exact opposite of
our situation, don't you?

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:28.330
Why is that?

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:31.000
Because even though I'm standing
so close to you, I feel like...

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.750
...you're the farthest thing away from me.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.840
I love you so much I can't stand it.

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:40.720
Yet here we are on a date, and I can't
even put my arm around your shoulder.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:42.010
A date?

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:45.760
Did you hear me say that earlier?

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:51.190
"I've always dreamed of coming into
town like this on a date with you."

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:53.940
Yeah, since you said that,

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:57.730
I hoped I could make this into one,
if only for a little while.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.740
But I couldn't do a thing.

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:03.030
I'm so sorry I couldn't show
you such a good time.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:05.370
I had a wonderful time.

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:10.290
It makes me happy just to be
by your side, Your Grace.

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:12.580
S-So, is that how you feel?

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.790
That's how I feel.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.840
I hope you'll continue to keep me near.

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:20.090
Even if we can never touch, Your Grace,

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:24.260
I'd like to get as close to you as I can
and gaze deep into your eyes.

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:30.850
I just remembered,

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:34.520
there's a festival going on in town today.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:37.980
Apparently, they're going to reenact the
princess and the moon's wedding.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.400
It could be pretty exciting.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.650
I couldn't care less.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:15:01.000
"If you cannot sleep, my master,
you are welcome in my room. -Alice"?

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:05.010
I wonder what she wants.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.890
That's her room, if I'm not mistaken.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:11.010
It's me. I saw your note, so I came here.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.020
Please, come in.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:16.150
Welcome to my room, Your Grace.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:17.980
Why the heck are you naked?!

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:20.860
When I'm in my room, I make it
a rule not to wear any clothes.

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:22.900
Well, I don't care! Put something on! Now!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.660
Thank you for waiting. Please, do come in.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:35.410
That outfit looks nice.
Hope I'm not disturbing you.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:38.960
What a pleasant fragrance!

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:43.340
I lit a scented candle.

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:48.090
Tonight, I thought I would ease
your tension, Your Grace.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:49.800
Ease my... Sounds kind of kinky!

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:52.100
I'll make you some tea.

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:54.180
Whoa! Calm down, now!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:56.890
Her morals have always been questionable.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:02.150
You're just overly aware of it because
you saw her naked a moment ago.

00:16:02.150 --> 00:16:03.440
Anyway, just cool your jets.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:08.320
What's this? Some strings? No...

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:11.120
A G-string?! What's it doing there?

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:13.330
I made you some chamomile tea.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:15.620
Please drink it while it's hot.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.500
Th-Thanks.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:25.510
Surely, she must be
wearing some underwear.

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:26.720
But knowing her...

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:29.470
When you're done with that,
let's head over to the bed.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:36.180
Is she planning on doing something to me?

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:40.900
All right, now take your
clothes off, please.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:45.940
Wh-What's she going to do?

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.110
We can't touch each other or anything.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.660
You have nothing to fear.

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:53.080
Just surrender yourself to me.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:55.450
She means business.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:16:59.960
Lie down, please.

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:01.170
Uh... all right.

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:06.420
What's she going to do to me?

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.380
Now close your eyes.

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:10.840
Let your mind and body relax.

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:14.390
All right, sweet dreams!

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:16.520
Huh?! You mean, go to sleep?!

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:20.480
Didn't you come here because
you were having trouble sleeping?

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:23.110
With the scented candle and chamomile tea,

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:29.530
I thought I could relax you somewhat
to help you fall asleep.

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:33.990
Please forgive me if I gave you
the wrong impression.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.530
She did this on purpose.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:38.410
Don't worry, Your Grace.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:41.250
I shall remain by your side
until you fall asleep.

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.300
Say, Alice...

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:51.590
Yes, Your Grace?

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:56.600
On the night after next, would you
mind going out with me for a bit?

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:58.470
There's something...

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.930
...I've got to show you.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.810
Something you've got to show me?

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.650
Yes, if you insist.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:35.590
So, this thing you wanted to show me...

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:39.310
...is a huge meteor shower
that happens once a decade?

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:45.230
Uh-huh. Ten years ago, I happened to see
it one night when I came out to this lake.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:48.020
What I saw that night,

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:49.900
I will always treasure.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:54.990
So, I wanted you to come along
with me and see it again.

00:18:54.990 --> 00:19:02.700
So, I get to have that wonderful
view and you all to myself, then.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.670
We came here to see the
shooting stars, of course.

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:09.420
But tonight, I want to tell you how
I really feel, sincerely for once...

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:11.840
...and not offhanded like I always do.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:13.510
And I'm determined to do it.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:18.180
The meteor shower should
begin any time now.

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:20.350
Alice, look up at the sky.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:21.350
All right.

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:25.270
I told you to look up at the sky.

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:28.270
It's more fun to look at you, Your Grace.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:30.820
Well, that's not why we're here.

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:34.150
Your hat!

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:39.870
Alice!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:46.710
Forgive me. It got a little wet.

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:49.790
It's okay, I don't mind.
Thanks for going out of your way.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.090
Now climb back on board.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:56.630
S-Sorry. I can't offer you my hand.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:59.050
If it weren't for this darn curse,

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:03.600
I wouldn't cause you and Rob
so much trouble.

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:05.060
I'm sorry for being this way.

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:09.060
If you can't touch me,

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.480
then give me a kiss.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:17.820
If you have any feelings for me,
then kiss me now.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:20.030
But you'll die.

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:24.410
Just think how romantic it would be
to die by your kiss, Your Grace.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:28.830
It's something the prince and
princess were never able to do.

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.260
D-Do you really want me to do it?

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:38.380
I want to kiss you, too, you know.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:43.560
If you keep saying stuff like that,
I'll do it for real.

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:46.560
I really want you to, Your Grace.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.740
I'm sorry, I just can't
go through with it.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:06.910
You said what I...

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:07.870
...thought you'd say.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:08.870
Wha--?!

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.550
Hey, you did that on purpose!

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:17.340
Forgive me, Your Grace.

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:23.680
You don't get enough exercise,
so I thought I'd force you to swim.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:26.100
Then just ask me to like a normal person!

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:29.480
It looks like the meteor shower is over.

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:30.560
Shall we head back?

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:32.350
Aw, man!

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.440
What a kick in the teeth!

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:39.780
I had a once-in-a-decade chance,
and now it's gone.

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:42.070
I couldn't even say what
I wanted to say to you.

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:43.700
What did you want to say to me?

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:46.490
I was going to tell you how
I really feel about you.

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:47.950
That I like you and all.

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.250
Er... I went and said it
in an offhanded way again.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:53.420
It doesn't ring true at all.

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:55.170
Oh, this is the pits!

00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:56.670
Let's go home now, Alice!

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:03.890
Yes, Your Grace.

00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:38.860
Your Grace?

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:45.780
Let's go back to that spot in another
ten years to watch the meteor shower.

00:23:45.780 --> 00:23:46.780
O-Okay.

00:23:47.490 --> 00:23:53.500
Does that mean she'll still be
with me ten years from now?

00:24:06.760 --> 00:24:10.180
"The Duke, Alice, and Memories of Snow."
